The paper, in Appendix C.3 and Table 4, describes an efficiency comparison between the "StateMask" explanation method and the proposed "Ours" explanation method. They report the cost time (in seconds) and number of samples used when training the mask network for each application, including the selfish mining environment.  
For the criterion to be satisfied, the submission must include actual code (not just instructions) that implements measuring training time during the training of the mask network for selfish mining using the "Ours" method. This could be done by wrapping the training loop with timing calls (e.g., `time.time()`, `time.perf_counter()`) and logging/printing the elapsed time, or by having a separate script that runs the training and records the duration. The presence of timing measurement code is necessary to reproduce the data shown in Table 4.

